WEBVTT

00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:15,090
If I run a short program, the first part of the night, and then start my cancer program,

00:00:15,810 --> 00:00:21,330
is the last two hours of that program the same as the first seven hours?

00:00:22,690 --> 00:00:30,450
So is the last two hours of my overnight program the same as the first seven hours? No.

00:00:31,410 --> 00:00:37,170
No, no, your night programs are running different frequencies throughout the nights.

00:00:37,170 --> 00:00:44,450
I mean, typically the maximum amount of time on any given frequency is only three minutes.

00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:52,610
So it's different going through that night. So if you're missing three,

00:00:52,610 --> 00:00:58,450
you know, a couple hours every single night, you know, there's nothing wrong with doing that

00:00:58,450 --> 00:01:02,450
for a period of time, but that's not best practice long-term.

